@startuml
title SysMon - Container Deployment Activity Diagram

|Admin (Tier 2 or 3)|
start
:Open Create Container;
:Select Visual Builder;
:Enter image repository tag;
:Select assigned Compute Group;
:Map persistent data to
assigned Storage Group folder;
:Select Docker or Podman;
:Click Deploy;

|SysMon Backend|
:Read container configuration;
:Validate Storage Group quota;

if (Storage Group quota exceeded?) then (Yes)
  :Halt Compose generation;
  :Notify admin that
  storage pool is full;
  stop
else (No)
  :Inject Compute Group
  resource limits;
  :Insert approved Storage Group
  host paths;
  :Generate docker-compose.yml;
endif

:Request deployment via
selected engine API;

|Container Engine|
if (Engine daemon reachable?) then (Yes)
  :Execute container deployment;
  :Start container;
  |SysMon Backend|
  :Begin streaming container telemetry;
  |Admin (Tier 2 or 3)|
  :View running container;
  stop
else (No)
  |SysMon Backend|
  :Save generated Compose file as draft;
  :Notify admin that engine
  daemon is unreachable;
  stop
endif

@enduml
